  questions:
  - questionText: What is a globe?
    options:
    - A spherical model of Earth
    - A flat map of one country
    - A model of the Moon
    - A weather instrument
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: Which imaginary line divides Earth into the Northern and Southern
      Hemispheres?
    options:
    - Prime Meridian
    - Equator
    - Tropic of Cancer
    - Arctic Circle
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: What do latitude lines measure?
    options:
    - Height above sea level
    - Distance east or west of the Prime Meridian
    - Distance north or south of the Equator
    - Distance between continents
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: What do longitude lines measure?
    options:
    - Distance north or south of the Equator
    - The depth of an ocean
    - The height of a mountain
    - Distance east or west of the Prime Meridian
    correctAnswerIndex: 3
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: At what longitude is the Prime Meridian located?
    options:
    - 0 degrees longitude
    - 23.5 degrees north
    - 66.5 degrees south
    - 180 degrees latitude
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: Where is the Tropic of Cancer located?
    options:
    - 23.5 degrees south
    - 23.5 degrees north
    - 66.5 degrees north
    - 0 degrees longitude
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: Where is the Tropic of Capricorn located?
    options:
    - 66.5 degrees south
    - 23.5 degrees north
    - 23.5 degrees south
    - 0 degrees latitude
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: Which pair correctly identifies the Polar Circles?
    options:
    - Equator and Prime Meridian
    - Tropic of Cancer and Tropic of Capricorn
    - North Pole and South Pole
    - Arctic Circle and Antarctic Circle
    correctAnswerIndex: 3
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: What causes day and night on Earth?
    options:
    - Earth's rotation on its axis
    - Earth's changing distance from the Sun
    - The Moon moving around Earth
    - Clouds blocking sunlight
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: What mainly causes the seasons on Earth?
    options:
    - The daily rotation of Earth
    - Earth's 23.5-degree axial tilt and revolution around the Sun
    - The movement of ocean water
    - The changing phases of the Moon
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: How many continents and major oceans are shown in this module?
    options:
    - Five continents and seven oceans
    - Six continents and four oceans
    - Seven continents and five oceans
    - Eight continents and six oceans
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: Which coordinates identify a precise location on Earth?
    options:
    - Altitude and temperature
    - Direction and speed
    - Time and distance
    - Latitude and longitude
    correctAnswerIndex: 3
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
